{"format":1,"seq":189,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm puzzled why the release run never triggered — branch pushes don't fire CI since it only runs on main, and tag pushes via the App token should normally work fine, so maybe there's a permissions issue with the token rather than an expiration problem.\n\nI also wonder who tagged v2.5.0 previously, since if a maintainer pushed earlier tags, the App's push events might somehow be getting ignored. Since I can't delete the tag, my best option is to manually create the draft release myself, replicating what release.yml does, and move the v2 tag — though that tag might also be protected, so I need to check how release.yml handles moving it with the github token before proceeding.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_01H8HqoZH4U9gg749WRBv6Nd","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Read rest of release.yml and v2.5.0 tagger\"}\nasync ({ shell: { exec } }) => (await exec(\"sed -n 30,200p .github/workflows/release.yml; git for-each-ref refs/tags/v2.5.0 refs/tags/v2.5.1 --format='%(refname) %(taggername) %(taggerdate)'\")).stdout"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","model":"aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":576,"cacheRead":27454,"cacheWrite":705,"totalTokens":28737,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":395},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794617982975,"responseId":"msg_bdrk_zvsvfpg5ax4e6xrotrrqpeb2hr44ep5gmunm2ac2fx3lk6457f7a","rawStopReason":"tool_use","durationMs":11109,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}],"kind":"pi.assistant","id":81,"conversationId":1,"byTaskId":80}},{"type":"task","value":{"id":80,"conversationId":1,"kind":"pi.generation","version":2,"input":{},"background":false,"abortRequested":false,"state":{"status":"waiting","checkpoint":{"phase":"tools","assist